-- title:
--   Inertia acts by the cyclotomic character on an ordinary corner
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime and $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ contain every unit mapping to $1$ under reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Let $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113): for every prime $\ell$ the geometric inputs `HeckeInputsHAlong` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ hold (definedness and integrality of the two Hecke maps, existence of principal divisors, finiteness along $\alpha$, the fundamental identity and the norm formula), and every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ is realised by a diamond automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$. Write $T =$ [`TateModule p (ModularCurve.JH M H)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of that function field with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra acting on $T$ compatibly with $\mathbb{Z}_p$ and faithfully, equipped with a map $\mathrm{op}$ from the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid M$) and $\langle d\rangle$ such that $\mathrm{op}(g)$ acts as `tateGenOpH` of $g$, and with $\mathbb{Z}_p[\mathrm{range}\,\mathrm{op}] = \mathbb{T}$. Let $(n, e_i, \mathfrak{m}_i)$ be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $\mathbb{T}$: complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$, maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ iff $i \ne j$; fix $i_0$ with $\mathrm{op}(U_p) \notin \mathfrak{m}_{i_0}$. Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits. Then for all $\sigma, \tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ attached to $Pl$ and all $x$ in the image of $e_{i_0}$ on $T$, one has $\rho(\tau)\bigl(\rho(\sigma)x - x\bigr) = \chi_{\mathrm{cyc},p}(\tau)\cdot\bigl(\rho(\sigma)x - x\bigr)$, where $\rho$ is the Galois action on $T$ and $\chi_{\mathrm{cyc},p}$ the $p$-adic cyclotomic character, its value taken in $\mathbb{Z}_p^\times \subseteq \mathbb{Z}_p$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the ordinary filtration of the $p$-adic Tate module at a prime exactly dividing the level: on the $e_{i_0}$-corner, the submodule generated by the elements $\rho(\sigma)x - x$ for $\sigma$ inertial lies in the part where inertia acts through the cyclotomic character, with no assertion about ranks, about the decomposition group, or about Frobenius. It feeds the construction of an adapted lattice basis, of the decomposition characters on the multiplicative submodule, and of the duality with supersingular polar differentials.
